<!-- P12 · Outgoing webhooks: queue per target (L4) -->
<Pattern
  id="p12"
  num="P12"
  lvl={4}
  titlePt={`Webhooks de saída: fila por endpoint`}
  titleEn={`Outgoing webhooks: queue per endpoint`}
  kickerPt={`Entregar em HTTP de terceiros que
            <em>falham, atrasam e quebram</em>. O segredo: isolar cada
            endpoint.`}
  kickerEn={`Delivering over HTTP to third parties that
            <em>fail, stall and break</em>. The trick: isolate each
            endpoint.`}
  tipPt={`<strong>Fale enquanto desenha:</strong> "Um evento pode ter N
              assinantes — o entregador cria um job de entrega <em>por
              endpoint</em>, um por fila. O worker assina com o secret HMAC do
              endpoint e faz o POST. 2xx? Apaga a mensagem. Falhou? Deixa sem
              ack e ela reaparece após o visibility timeout — o backoff é do
              worker, ajustando visibility/delay. No maxReceiveCount o SQS
              redrive à DLQ. Fila própria + limite de concorrência/rate por
              endpoint: um cliente fora do ar não esgota os workers. Assine
              timestamp + eventId + payload e rejeite replay."`}
  tipEn={`<strong>Say while drawing:</strong> "One event may have N
              subscribers — the delivery service creates a delivery job
              <em>per endpoint</em>, one per queue. The worker signs with the
              endpoint's HMAC secret and sends the POST. 2xx? Delete the
              message. Failure? Leave it unacknowledged and it reappears after
              the visibility timeout — backoff is worker-controlled, adjusting
              visibility/delay. At maxReceiveCount SQS redrives to the DLQ.
              Own queue plus per-endpoint concurrency/rate limits: one outage
              can't exhaust every worker. HMAC-sign timestamp + eventId +
              payload, and reject replays."`}
  whyPt={`<strong>Por quê SQS e não Kafka:</strong> a falha é
              <em>por mensagem, por endpoint</em>. SQS fornece visibility
              timeout e redrive para DLQ; o backoff é definido pela aplicação.
              Filas por endpoint + limites de concorrência isolam falhas.
              <em>Tradeoff:</em> pool compartilhado de workers enfraquece o
              isolamento — endpoint A pode consumir toda a capacidade; use
              limites de concorrência/rate ou capacidade reservada por
              endpoint. DLQ por endpoint, ou preserve endpointId, tentativas e
              erro numa DLQ compartilhada. At-least-once → o receptor tolera
              duplicata via eventId (delivery ID); HMAC autentica, timestamp +
              eventId evitam replay.`}
  whyEn={`<strong>Why SQS, not Kafka:</strong> failure is
              <em>per message, per endpoint</em>. SQS provides visibility
              timeout and DLQ redrive; the application defines backoff timing.
              Per-endpoint queues plus concurrency limits isolate failures.
              <em>Tradeoff:</em> a shared worker pool weakens isolation —
              endpoint A can consume all capacity; use per-endpoint
              concurrency/rate limits or reserved capacity. Prefer a DLQ per
              endpoint, or preserve endpointId, attempt count and error in a
              shared DLQ. At-least-once means the receiver deduplicates by
              eventId (delivery ID); HMAC authenticates, while timestamp +
              eventId prevent replay.`}
>
